7.8 support — retained GPU atlas storage
Authorization: 66a95d56. Profile read: .bboxy/runs/r2b-profile.log.
Order: after x-height d8f2b86, before paths and complete GraphTab.

Mechanism:
chrome/mod.rs ChromeRenderer::with_context — immutable icon GPU texture/view
and its linear sampler created once per renderer/device; CPU icon pixels and
pixel-coordinate metadata unchanged.
chrome/mod.rs text-cache miss — retain inserted AtlasRect as dirty, then sync
once before a flat draw. Warm passes and material-separated draws reuse storage.
chrome/atlas_gpu.rs — first use/growth full-uploads the glyph atlas and increments
the texture generation; otherwise queue.write_texture covers only dirty rects.
Transparent guard texels stay zero. Bind groups retain old generations through
already-encoded work. No uniform/storage arena, font, shader or material tuning.

Tests:
- repeated isolated passes: exact fresh/cached RGBA, icon uploads=1, no warm
  glyph writes or bytes;
- dirty insert: sub-atlas upload; growth: preserved coordinates, exact RGBA
  against a fresh renderer;
- growth in a later group: earlier encoded text remains correct after replacing
  its atlas generation (actual GPU readback, not only a counter assertion).

